  "semantic_contract": "Connected native input/display/panel producer-consumer contracts. Amiga D170 reads mirrored CIAA PRA bit6 active-low into201 and POTINP bit10 active-low into202; alternate packet3B61E writes corresponding button bits1/0.201 drives menu/cancel/start and202 selects mouse-Y speed versus rotation behavior. D170 stores JOY0DAT low/high BYTEs in1FF/200 after signed wrap-delta extraction; viewer initializes those counters and original random-mix38C8 reads them. Their meaning is hardware counter samples, not screen coordinates. BYTE20A is a bitmask: bit0 gates reticle sprite drawing and follows internal/external view; bit1 gates resource HUD; signbit gates selected IRQ motion/message/panel-counter services, whilezero/nonzero gates other services. Preserve startup7F/latebit7/80/0/0E states, not one Boolean or globalpause. BYTE209 is a consumed request: resource-contact/charging and volcano paths set it; panel updater sets reload WORDs3/4 tozero and clears request, else100. WORD7C2 increments in nonmodal signed20A IRQ branch and panel updater tests low BYTE against5 then clears wholeWORD. Not universal frames, no new runtime or physical left/right assertion beyond original primary/secondary button roles. Current canonical base assumptions remain conditional; byte exactness does not establish every input path.",
